cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite godot-sandbox.
title: godot-sandbox guest API and cmake helper (vendored)
abstract: >-
  The C++ guest API (program/cpp/docker/api) and the add_sandbox_program cmake
  helper (program/cpp/cmake) from the org's godot-sandbox fork. This is
  everything a guest ELF needs to build against; the runtime addon is
  separate (project/addons/godot_sandbox). Local adaptations: the cmake
  example directory is omitted; and docker/api/native.cpp's aligned
  allocation is rewritten. Upstream's memalign (behind posix_memalign,
  aligned_alloc and aligned operator new) retried malloc up to 16 times for
  an aligned block and, when every try missed, returned the last block after
  freeing it, so the caller held freed memory and a later free was a double
  free (Gate 4: "Possible double-free" in Geogram's ~Delaunay3d; at 4096
  alignment nearly every call missed). Now memalign over-allocates by
  alignment - 1 and returns the aligned address inside the block; a small
  open-addressing table maps each such address to the host block, and
  free/realloc (the --wrap targets, which become C functions around the
  renamed free/realloc syscalls) consult it first. The table is freed when
  no aligned block is live. posix_memalign answers EINVAL/ENOMEM instead of
  1. Gate 0F probe 17 (gates/0f-runtime) checks 3000 blocks at 64/128/4096
  alignment against a copy of the old fallback. And in the --wrap build,
  __wrap_memset/memcpy/memmove/memcmp are C functions that split a span into
  16 MiB pieces over the bare syscalls: the host views at most 16 MiB of
  guest memory per memory syscall, and ggml's test-backend-ops copies 64 MiB
  tensors (Gate 3, a protection fault above 16 MiB).
type: software
authors:
